        "title": "Introduction",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Let&#x27;s take a number, say, <span class=\"math\">[MATH: -3.]</span> We can depict it on a number line as follows:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Let's take a number, say, [MATH: -3.] We can depict it on a number line as follows:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "graphic",
            "normalized_html": "<p><img src=\"/graphics/639fbaffa133fb983eef5d2453eeedba\"></p>",
            "readable_text": "[IMG: /graphics/639fbaffa133fb983eef5d2453eeedba]",
            "images": [
              {
                "src": "/graphics/639fbaffa133fb983eef5d2453eeedba",
                "alt": ""
              }
            ],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>The <em>distance</em> between the number <span class=\"math\">[MATH: -3]</span> and <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 0]</span> is known as the <strong>absolute value</strong> of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: -3.]</span> We write it as\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: |-3| = {\\color{red}3}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "The distance between the number [MATH: -3] and [MATH: 0] is known as the absolute value of [MATH: -3.] We write it as\n[MATH: |-3| = {\\color{red}3}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Similarly, <span class=\"math\">[MATH: |\\,2\\,|]</span>, the absolute value of the number <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2]</span>, is the distance between <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2]</span> and <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 0]</span>:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Similarly, [MATH: |\\,2\\,|], the absolute value of the number [MATH: 2], is the distance between [MATH: 2] and [MATH: 0]:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "graphic",
            "normalized_html": "<p><img src=\"/graphics/197c5c28024cc300e7086bfff10e313a\"></p>",
            "readable_text": "[IMG: /graphics/197c5c28024cc300e7086bfff10e313a]",
            "images": [
              {
                "src": "/graphics/197c5c28024cc300e7086bfff10e313a",
                "alt": ""
              }
            ],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We write <span class=\"math\">[MATH: |\\,2\\,| = {\\color{red}2}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We write [MATH: |\\,2\\,| = {\\color{red}2}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>So, the absolute value simply </p>",
            "readable_text": "So, the absolute value simply",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<ul><li><p><em>removes the minus sign</em>, if the number is negative, or</p></li><li><p>does nothing, if the number is non-negative.</p></li></ul>",
            "readable_text": "- removes the minus sign, if the number is negative, or\n- does nothing, if the number is non-negative.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Sometimes, we can be asked to evaluate an expression involving the absolute value function, like <span class=\"math\">[MATH: |x +1| + 5]</span> when <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x=-3.]</span> In this case, we evaluate the expression inside the absolute value before simplifying the rest of the expression: \n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: |x + 1|+ 5|=;|(\u2212 3) + 1|+ 5|=;|\u2212 2|+ 5|=; 2 + 5|=; 7]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Sometimes, we can be asked to evaluate an expression involving the absolute value function, like [MATH: |x +1| + 5] when [MATH: x=-3.] In this case, we evaluate the expression inside the absolute value before simplifying the rest of the expression:\n[MATH: |x + 1|+ 5|=;|(\u2212 3) + 1|+ 5|=;|\u2212 2|+ 5|=; 2 + 5|=; 7]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [
          {
            "src": "/graphics/639fbaffa133fb983eef5d2453eeedba",
            "alt": ""
          },
